{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he shall bring that which is for the sin-offering first.</b> The sin-offering precedes the burnt-offering (Sifra). To what may the matter be compared? To an advocate who enters to appease — once the advocate has appeased, the gift enters after him (Zevachim 7)." "<b>And he shall not divide it.</b> He nicks only one sign (Ḥullin 21)." "<b>The neck.</b> It is the upper part of the head that slopes toward the side of the neck." "<b>From the side of his neck.</b> Opposite the one who sees the back of the neck — and it is the entire length of the back of the neck (ibid. 19)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "Rashi refers to the melikah cut; 'one sign' means cutting either the trachea or the esophagus, not both."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:02.777318040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}